WEBVTT

01:27.140 --> 01:29.980
<b>AQUARION</b>

01:32.380 --> 01:33.850
This place...

01:36.410 --> 01:37.700
I know it.

01:41.460 --> 01:42.680
I'm sure.

01:51.360 --> 01:52.660
Are you...

01:53.960 --> 01:55.220
me?

01:59.420 --> 02:00.870
Senpai!

02:00.870 --> 02:02.720
Momohime-senpai!

02:04.930 --> 02:07.330
Momohime-senpai!

02:07.330 --> 02:07.940
Huh?

02:08.940 --> 02:12.100
Why am I in the infirmary?

02:12.100 --> 02:14.050
You passed out in the library.

02:15.190 --> 02:17.830
I remember a time...

02:18.550 --> 02:22.670
You aren't supposed to 
die before I kill you!

02:23.540 --> 02:25.720
It's okay, Hana-chan.

02:27.390 --> 02:29.620
I made you a promise, didn't I?

02:34.830 --> 02:37.550
The nurse said she was probably just anemic.

02:37.990 --> 02:39.880
Maybe he did something to her.

02:39.880 --> 02:41.980
He who? Sun-kun?

02:42.410 --> 02:45.380
It isn't right to accuse 
people without evidence.

02:45.380 --> 02:48.390
What, are you guys taking his side now, too?

02:48.390 --> 02:50.600
No, we're not trying to.

02:51.290 --> 02:55.780
But when we got there, 
Momohime-senpai was all alone.

02:58.940 --> 03:01.510
Sorry. I'm going for a run.

03:25.380 --> 03:27.260
Sakko, flank right!

03:27.260 --> 03:28.680
O-Okay!

03:28.680 --> 03:30.680
Rimiya-kun, fly out from behind me!

03:30.680 --> 03:31.340
All right!

03:35.360 --> 03:36.460
<i>Got it!</i>

03:36.460 --> 03:37.310
Nice, Rimiya!

03:39.080 --> 03:42.620
Wow, they beat it without uniting!

03:46.620 --> 03:49.090
Looks like Momohime-senpai is all right.

03:49.090 --> 03:50.220
Ya.

03:52.050 --> 03:57.090
Amaha-san, you still aren't back to 
normal yet. Your mana value stayed low.

03:57.090 --> 03:59.750
Oh, did it? I'm sorry.

03:59.750 --> 04:03.890
Otori-kun, your mana value was unstable 
and kept fluctuating the whole time.

04:03.890 --> 04:05.110
You can't unite like that.

04:05.110 --> 04:06.260
Whaddya expect me—

04:06.810 --> 04:08.600
Let's stop here for today.

04:09.610 --> 04:11.930
Don't worry. We'll do better next time.

04:14.600 --> 04:18.110
I'm so glad Momohime-neesama 
is all better now.

04:18.110 --> 04:19.930
Wait a second. 
What do you mean "neesama"?

04:19.930 --> 04:23.110
She was really on her game. 
Almost better than before.

04:23.110 --> 04:25.940
Her mana value was still low though.

04:25.940 --> 04:28.020
Yeah, but so was yours, Sakko.

04:28.020 --> 04:31.040
That's right. Did you have 
something on your mind?

04:31.300 --> 04:32.700
Nah, it's nothing—

04:35.370 --> 04:36.500
What's wrong?

04:36.500 --> 04:37.970
F-Forget it.

04:41.260 --> 04:46.130
...ver universe, overwhelmed by tears...

04:46.880 --> 04:54.010
...ld universe, enveloped in flames...

04:52.570 --> 04:54.000
What's that about?

04:55.230 --> 04:59.150
We gather to think about the state 
of the universe together. Join us!

04:58.040 --> 04:59.150
It is quite fun.

04:59.150 --> 05:03.140
Let's look at the stars together and have 
a conversation about the universe.

05:03.390 --> 05:05.050
Whassup with them?

05:05.050 --> 05:06.650
They are pawns of the space aliens.

05:06.970 --> 05:09.160
S-Space aliens?

05:09.160 --> 05:10.500
They get signals.

05:10.500 --> 05:14.860
They receive signals from space 
and act as they're ordered!

05:15.210 --> 05:17.660
Th-That sounds scary.

05:17.920 --> 05:22.330
Catastrophes and pandemics. 
Wars and political instability.

05:22.640 --> 05:24.870
These tragedies keep occurring

05:24.870 --> 05:28.260
because the world is controlled 
by a shadow government!

05:28.260 --> 05:32.690
Oh, how foolish mankind is!

05:33.390 --> 05:37.190
They work in the darkness, advancing 
their plan to destroy the world.

05:37.190 --> 05:37.980
Huh?

05:38.390 --> 05:42.190
H-How come you know about that?

05:42.450 --> 05:45.220
Their voices fall to me.

05:45.930 --> 05:47.200
Fall to you?

05:47.560 --> 05:51.650
"Universe." "Union." "Destruction."

05:52.000 --> 05:54.790
When the two universes collide,

05:53.910 --> 05:54.790
Oh?

05:55.090 --> 05:59.220
all will be destroyed. All will disappear!

06:01.820 --> 06:06.070
You mean you all knew about them? 
About the space aliens?

06:06.070 --> 06:07.890
Knew? Not exactly.

06:07.890 --> 06:11.000
Hana-chan, that guy is called Kamisama.

06:11.000 --> 06:11.870
You mean like God?!

06:11.870 --> 06:14.380
Yeah, but listen, it's just a nickname.

06:14.380 --> 06:17.300
You really shouldn't believe what he says.

06:17.300 --> 06:18.550
Oh, really?

06:18.550 --> 06:23.820
Still, if you think about it, aren't those 
things we fight basically space aliens?

06:23.820 --> 06:24.280
Huh?

06:24.280 --> 06:25.410
Yeah.

06:25.410 --> 06:30.420
Sun-kun talked about the Mythic Beasts 
like they were people who had emotions.

06:30.420 --> 06:34.990
Say what? Really? Hey, tell me!

06:36.320 --> 06:38.130
It's lunch now, right?

06:38.130 --> 06:39.330
Huh? Yeah.

06:39.640 --> 06:42.540
So why is nobody here?

06:42.540 --> 06:47.660
You know, I haven't seen a lot 
of people around recently.

07:13.070 --> 07:16.420
That's when I heard a voice.

07:16.420 --> 07:18.790
I will kill you now.

07:19.310 --> 07:25.130
If they're saying they'll "kill" us, 
that means we're killing them too, right?

07:25.680 --> 07:28.290
Even though they are space aliens.

07:28.620 --> 07:30.000
Mm-hmm.

07:30.000 --> 07:33.710
The fear of death manifests 
in the illusion of an enemy.

07:33.710 --> 07:37.810
You must dispel the illusion 
and think with your own head.

07:37.810 --> 07:40.890
If you do that, the true 
enemy will be revealed.

07:40.890 --> 07:43.250
With my own head...

07:43.250 --> 07:44.170
Mm-hmm.

07:44.930 --> 07:48.970
Then you must act in accordance 
with your beliefs,

07:48.970 --> 07:52.170
regardless of the outcome that produces.

07:52.910 --> 07:55.420
That is what justice is.

07:58.660 --> 07:59.500
A dream?

07:59.500 --> 08:00.810
Yeah.

08:00.810 --> 08:06.160
I'm in some familiar, mysterious place, 
and I meet this wonderful person.

08:06.670 --> 08:10.310
At first, I thought it was this 
past me that I keep seeing,

08:10.310 --> 08:12.850
but something was different about it.

08:12.850 --> 08:17.340
Dreams are the myths that mana shows you 
when it resonates with the universe.

08:17.340 --> 08:19.860
Myths that mana shows you?

08:19.860 --> 08:22.790
What is Momohime-senpai up to anyway?

08:22.790 --> 08:23.820
Who knows?

08:27.960 --> 08:28.970
Watch out!

08:32.360 --> 08:34.040
Give Yoko back to me!

08:35.450 --> 08:36.280
Momo-nee!

08:36.530 --> 08:37.380
Yeah!

08:39.030 --> 08:44.390
It's your fault. It's all your 
fault that Yoko went crazy!

08:45.630 --> 08:48.020
Give Yoko and Satoshi back!

08:53.620 --> 08:54.680
Could this be...

08:57.050 --> 09:01.020
Don't worry. You will be 
one with them eventually.

09:04.410 --> 09:05.790
Are you all right, Sun?

09:05.790 --> 09:07.530
It's Yoko-san's father.

09:07.530 --> 09:08.740
Again?

09:08.740 --> 09:12.420
Are you kids hurt at all? 
We'll take care of the rest.

09:13.100 --> 09:16.540
I'll take you back to your wife. Come on.

09:20.520 --> 09:21.940
Who are those people?

09:22.490 --> 09:25.990
Like me, they are people 
who dream of the egg.

09:26.350 --> 09:29.240
You want to become one 
with me too, don't you?

09:29.240 --> 09:31.330
What? It's not like that!

09:38.050 --> 09:41.010
Amaha-san is fine physically,

09:41.010 --> 09:43.080
but for some reason her mana 
value isn't increasing.

09:47.040 --> 09:50.430
You want to become one 
with me too, don't you?

09:52.240 --> 09:54.970
But I never expected 
Otori-kun to get even worse.

09:56.470 --> 09:58.040
That's enough for today.

09:58.040 --> 10:01.540
Amaha-san, Otori-kun, get plenty of rest 
and try to conserve your strength.

10:02.540 --> 10:03.950
Okay.

10:10.530 --> 10:14.540
Hey. So, what's really going on with you two?

10:14.540 --> 10:15.430
What do you mean?

10:15.670 --> 10:17.920
Why do you always walk home together?

10:18.290 --> 10:19.340
I like him.

10:19.340 --> 10:20.010
Huh?

10:20.010 --> 10:24.090
Well, my intuition tells 
me he's not a bad person.

10:24.510 --> 10:27.020
When we're together, 
I get this strange feeling.

10:27.370 --> 10:29.450
One I've never felt before.

10:29.950 --> 10:31.360
I wonder if it's love.

10:31.690 --> 10:34.120
But you aren't...

10:34.120 --> 10:38.680
Yeah, it can't be, can it? 
I'm not supposed to be able to love.

10:38.680 --> 10:39.820
Right, right.

10:40.980 --> 10:44.860
But anyway, do you have a 
crush on anyone, Sakko?

10:44.860 --> 10:45.540
Hah?!

10:45.540 --> 10:49.300
Oh, you do? Then your big 
sis here will back you up.

10:49.300 --> 10:52.190
Who is it? Who? Come on, come on, come on!

10:51.230 --> 10:52.610
Shut up!

10:53.440 --> 10:57.420
That must be nice. 
I wish I could fall in love, too.

10:57.730 --> 10:59.000
Are you serious?

10:59.000 --> 11:02.770
Rimiya says he fell deep in love before.

11:02.770 --> 11:04.230
Yeah, I bet.

11:04.830 --> 11:07.720
I wonder if Toshi-kun likes anybody.

11:08.330 --> 11:11.260
I don't think he's been 
in love before either.

11:11.260 --> 11:12.330
Why not?

11:11.270 --> 11:15.020
<b>Hiroshi | Shinobu</b>

11:12.700 --> 11:14.490
Just doesn't seem like it.

11:15.020 --> 11:16.540
I guess.

11:17.420 --> 11:20.030
Love sure is complicated.

11:21.000 --> 11:25.530
How old do you think you 
have to be to fall in love?

11:25.970 --> 11:27.740
Why are you asking that?

11:28.540 --> 11:33.790
You know, when I was a kid, 
I used to think that you liked Sayo.

11:34.720 --> 11:35.470
Uh...

11:36.290 --> 11:38.040
And I was sure that Sayo...

11:40.300 --> 11:42.490
Anyway, see you tomorrow!

11:46.360 --> 11:48.620
Hey, where are we going?

11:48.620 --> 11:51.760
Somewhere nice. Sun-kun is waiting for us.

11:51.760 --> 11:54.320
It's really comforting there.

12:06.370 --> 12:07.490
Wha—?

12:33.750 --> 12:36.420
What the hell have you done?

12:36.420 --> 12:37.180
Not a thing.

12:37.180 --> 12:41.190
What's wrong with them? 
Did you hypnotize them or something?

12:42.260 --> 12:47.190
They are all dreaming as they 
resonate with the universe.

12:51.660 --> 12:52.570
Oh!

12:53.870 --> 12:54.910
Huh?

13:15.650 --> 13:18.030
And now they have all gone.

13:18.030 --> 13:20.260
What kind of magic trick is this?

13:20.260 --> 13:24.770
All I'm doing is tuning everyone's mana.

13:25.070 --> 13:27.480
Tuning mana?

13:28.070 --> 13:32.700
Emotions are bound by space-time, 
so mana cannot be free.

13:33.520 --> 13:37.620
Everyone is covering their ears 
to the voice of their mana.

13:37.620 --> 13:40.140
Is that how you tricked Momohime?!

13:53.550 --> 13:54.340
Wha—?

13:55.360 --> 13:56.740
Huh?

13:59.100 --> 14:00.320
Where's Sakko?

14:00.320 --> 14:00.980
Dunno.

14:00.980 --> 14:02.840
Otori isn't here?

14:02.840 --> 14:05.490
It shouldn't be a problem, Vice Principal.

14:05.830 --> 14:11.040
DEAVA is saying that 
Tsukishiro Rimiya-kun, Hatano Toshi-kun,

14:11.040 --> 14:14.470
and Ichiki Hana-kun will 
form the team this time.

14:14.870 --> 14:17.700
Amaha-san, it seems your mana 
gauge still isn't high enough.

14:17.700 --> 14:18.550
You'll stay on standby.

14:18.970 --> 14:20.190
All right.

14:21.790 --> 14:23.790
I wonder what happened to Sakko.

14:23.790 --> 14:26.760
It's within 15 kilometers from
 Ashigaratoge Pass and the stake at Hakone.

14:26.760 --> 14:29.230
If they place a second stake, 
they'll only be one step away!

14:29.600 --> 14:31.890
You absolutely must stop it!

14:32.140 --> 14:32.990
All right!

14:33.870 --> 14:37.220
This is a cradle for eggs 
that are waiting to hatch.

14:37.220 --> 14:42.620
They are simply waiting for the eggs to 
crack open and all of you to finally spring out.

14:43.550 --> 14:44.830
What the hell is going on?

14:47.680 --> 14:48.600
Sayo!

14:49.420 --> 14:51.060
Oh. It's just Hana.

14:51.600 --> 14:52.810
No, it isn't!

15:07.900 --> 15:08.950
Sayo!

15:10.720 --> 15:11.740
Sayo.

15:12.340 --> 15:13.300
I'm sorry.

15:17.070 --> 15:19.210
I... about before.

15:21.880 --> 15:22.890
Wait!

15:26.980 --> 15:28.850
What's happening?

15:35.570 --> 15:39.330
It's shaped like a person.

15:41.580 --> 15:44.710
The head will be
 Ichiki Hana-kun in Vector Feoh.

15:45.700 --> 15:47.640
Hana-chan, do your best!

15:48.080 --> 15:50.200
W-Will do!

15:51.770 --> 15:54.860
Mythic Star Union! Go, Aquarion!

16:06.860 --> 16:12.110
Oh, sick! This really does feel good.

16:25.800 --> 16:28.960
Take care not to touch the 
Mythic Beast's tentacles.

16:28.960 --> 16:31.890
Use Aquarion Feoh's bow and arrows.

16:31.890 --> 16:33.910
Uh, all right.

16:43.890 --> 16:45.900
Nice one! Take another shot!

16:45.900 --> 16:46.810
Yeah!

16:49.120 --> 16:51.160
This isn't a good reaction!

16:52.120 --> 16:52.980
<i>Huh?</i>

17:06.220 --> 17:08.450
Place a 500-meter radius 
blockade around the stake!

17:08.450 --> 17:09.940
Evacuate the residents!

17:09.940 --> 17:13.170
We can still nullify the stake! 
Defeat the Mythic Beast!

17:13.490 --> 17:14.450
<i>All right!</i>

17:15.680 --> 17:18.570
Why do you guys kill Mythic Beasts

17:18.840 --> 17:20.730
when you don't even love them?

17:22.090 --> 17:24.970
If that brings you pleasure, so be it.

17:24.970 --> 17:27.230
If it brings pain, it is unforgivable.

17:27.670 --> 17:30.210
Momo-nee! Sayo! Where are you?

17:30.210 --> 17:34.970
<i>Emotions are bound by space-time, 
so mana cannot be free.</i>

17:34.970 --> 17:39.080
<i>Everyone is covering their ears 
to the voice of their mana.</i>

17:39.920 --> 17:41.030
Am I...

17:42.120 --> 17:44.590
inside my own mana?

17:47.020 --> 17:50.850
Don't worry. I'll be 
scared for you instead.

17:55.690 --> 17:56.720
Hey.

18:05.540 --> 18:07.800
<i>Nice, Hana-chan! Just like that!</i>

18:08.290 --> 18:09.740
<i>Got it!</i>

18:23.870 --> 18:25.610
<i>Kill me.</i>

18:27.320 --> 18:28.800
The enemy is talking again.

18:29.250 --> 18:32.660
<i>You have won. Kill me.</i>

18:34.720 --> 18:40.020
It really is a human, isn't it?

18:42.330 --> 18:43.810
This isn't good.

18:43.810 --> 18:45.790
Ichiki-san, shoot it now!

18:58.370 --> 18:59.590
<i>Hana-chan!</i>

18:59.590 --> 19:02.190
<i>If we don't beat it now, 
the stake will remain!</i>

19:02.190 --> 19:06.620
<i>Why do you hesitate? Kill me!</i>

19:08.870 --> 19:12.150
You must act in accordance with your beliefs,

19:12.150 --> 19:15.370
regardless of the outcome that produces.

19:15.370 --> 19:17.950
That is what justice is.

19:19.610 --> 19:20.930
Hana-chan!

19:28.480 --> 19:29.560
What?!

19:31.390 --> 19:33.480
There's no way I could kill someone

19:34.670 --> 19:36.660
I don't even like.

19:50.750 --> 19:52.320
Blessings of the Goddess.

19:52.320 --> 19:54.260
Blessings of the Goddess.

19:54.870 --> 19:56.660
Blessings of the Goddess.

19:58.720 --> 20:00.670
Blessings of the Goddess.

20:15.040 --> 20:16.300
You there.

20:21.490 --> 20:23.480
You should have caught this first.

20:23.480 --> 20:25.430
But you are the one who did.

20:25.760 --> 20:27.310
How cowardly.

20:27.310 --> 20:31.270
You are so afraid of conflict that 
you cannot take what you want.

20:31.780 --> 20:32.470
Yes.

20:32.870 --> 20:36.950
People call me Nanook the Coward.

20:37.250 --> 20:37.920
Oh...

20:46.250 --> 20:48.190
Nanook the Coward.

20:49.990 --> 20:52.300
That is your best quality.

21:09.220 --> 21:12.810
Promise. Universe. Union.

21:12.810 --> 21:17.890
Proof of vows. A seal. A reunion.

21:18.220 --> 21:23.920
Birth. A holy egg. 
Twelve thousand years.

21:40.780 --> 21:43.170
I wonder if Hana-chan is okay.

21:43.170 --> 21:47.350
Momohime-neesama got worried and tried to 
talk to her, but she pretty much ran off.

21:48.150 --> 21:49.350
Sakko!

21:50.360 --> 21:53.590
Why didn't you show up? 
We were all summoned.

21:54.480 --> 21:55.850
Sakko?

21:57.810 --> 21:58.820
Oh, crap.

21:59.520 --> 22:00.380
Huh?

22:00.830 --> 22:03.760
I think I might actually

22:05.300 --> 22:06.620
like him.

22:07.640 --> 22:08.820
Huh?!
